Subject: screenshot: correctly detect hardware frames before CPU conversion

Backport of mpv-player/mpv commit c66204b69ba201cf6611daae7e515442eed4b9cd:
https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/commit/c66204b69ba201cf6611daae7e515442eed4b9cd

In mpv 0.41.0, mp_image_sethwfmt() fills image->fmt from the software
subformat (NV12/P010), so fmt.flags no longer identifies a hardware image.
Check image->imgfmt instead and let mp_image_hw_download() download only
the requested screenshot. Playback stays on direct d3d11va; no decoder
mode or rendering configuration is changed.

diff --git a/player/screenshot.c b/player/screenshot.c
--- a/player/screenshot.c
+++ b/player/screenshot.c
@@ -377,7 +377,7 @@ static struct mp_image *screenshot_get(struct MPContext *mpctx, int mode,
     }
 
     // vo_get_current_frame() can return a hardware frame, which we have to download first.
-    if (image && image->fmt.flags & MP_IMGFLAG_HWACCEL) {
+    if (image && IMGFMT_IS_HWACCEL(image->imgfmt)) {
         struct mp_image *nimage = mp_image_hw_download(image, NULL);
         talloc_free(image);
         if (!nimage)
